    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 288,
        "text": "Welcome back to the Thursday planning panel. I'm Maya Chen, and today we're comparing how three teams adapt when plans change. With me are Daniel Ortiz from the events team, Priya Nair from logistics, and Sam Lee from customer support. Daniel, start us off. What happened last week?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "05b8295f79deb8c7b4b22b2805c8d08ee9eca821f00b0ffb62eb8b2885ea7ebe",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 298,
        "sourceEnd": 771,
        "text": "Sure. We planned a two-day training for forty people. On Monday morning, the venue called and said the main room was flooded. We had only four hours to move everything. My first idea was to cancel, but the team said no. We moved to a smaller room and split the group into two sessions. It worked, but the sound was bad in the afternoon, so some people couldn't hear the speakers properly. The smaller room also meant we had to rearrange seating quickly, which added stress.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "90ecbaff8a8de2d17bd35d4d987a6d235d89d78903d61f5efbbdbb64d45db069",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 779,
        "sourceEnd": 812,
        "text": "Priya, how did logistics respond?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "f0866332d794bf8c3ef59db2d5357c6fc83367ac679d7fdacb881ffcc59bca2f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 821,
        "sourceEnd": 1152,
        "text": "We had two trucks and fifteen boxes of materials. When Daniel called, we sent one truck to the new room and kept one at the old venue. That was a mistake, actually. The second truck waited for ninety minutes and did nothing. Next time, we will send both trucks immediately and decide later. That way, we avoid delays and confusion.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "1d2f431a540145ea71e04b87476a8e1b4c7faa45436b6bc6df00ac04c1da978c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "sam",
        "speaker": "Sam",
        "sourceStart": 1159,
        "sourceEnd": 1511,
        "text": "From support, we saw a different problem. Twelve people called to ask about the room change. Our phone line had only two staff. We recorded a short message in English and Chinese, and the calls dropped to five in one hour. So clear information helped more than extra staff. It showed that a simple, multilingual message can reduce pressure on the team.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "3101328d9ca30e0e95a82aa7d62a0794374f880107d8c1a692f1dc889bae897b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1519,
        "sourceEnd": 1570,
        "text": "Interesting. Daniel, what would you do differently?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "67ecb6b9a22d863c367b73105876387952cbbf2f2b169225beb09751ea070c9f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1580,
        "sourceEnd": 1842,
        "text": "Three things. First, we need a backup room list, not just one room. Second, we should test the sound equipment before eight in the morning. Third, we must tell speakers about changes before they arrive, not after. These steps would prevent the problems we faced.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "563f8fd2c9b7bd37128a3721909a7b4f0e7bad723bc7f711664dc5da2c982795",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1850,
        "sourceEnd": 1870,
        "text": "Priya, do you agree?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "f2f4f6d86d575f331b2d7e8c1d4889b3a36bb4c4a946c7da4a3cb1789bc22a23",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1879,
        "sourceEnd": 2176,
        "text": "Mostly. But I want to add one point. We should name one person as the decision maker. Last week, three people gave different instructions, and the truck drivers were confused. One driver went to the wrong building. It cost us forty minutes. Having a single decision maker would avoid such mix-ups.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b01a3e998586a9a8781b404ebe1d8eb13c0ff4a406e648a78ff07d20336b226b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "sam",
        "speaker": "Sam",
        "sourceStart": 2183,
        "sourceEnd": 2434,
        "text": "I agree with Priya. In support, we also need one clear script. People asked, \"Is the training still on?\" and \"Where is the new room?\" We gave different answers at first. That was not good. A standard script ensures everyone gives the same information.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "b5cf7c9af50c93c25e579a776b4dcf014bf00812d9642234c09585a015aa74ae",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2442,
        "sourceEnd": 2571,
        "text": "So the panel agrees on three strategies: a backup plan, one decision maker, and one clear message. Daniel, is there a cost issue?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "f4c7c60602f16c4cb43fae25df7584ec8638270089f33eae78ddf975b2db8034",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2581,
        "sourceEnd": 2766,
        "text": "Yes. The new room cost two hundred dollars more. But canceling would cost more, maybe one thousand dollars in refunds. So the change was cheaper. In the end, we saved money by adapting.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "5e7f1484eec4484a4745ec539439e4d580b437b7055bc6c70dae73c1c4e20a46",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2774,
        "sourceEnd": 2798,
        "text": "Priya, any final number?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "772e0c31e2f33741d6efd8221a864b7b4b9e17fa0d085502f60ef72bae7401c0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2807,
        "sourceEnd": 2955,
        "text": "We lost forty minutes with the truck, but we saved the event. I think that is a good trade. The time lost was small compared to the overall success.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "8c481b4e4bc6de195a91da8f86736d0460768508ecf14df686e01ba899ca9546",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2963,
        "sourceEnd": 2978,
        "text": "Sam, last word?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d1e2b69512c1a633e3fe8e29a6e6e815c499f6860b0ecbb677875fc5715fb81f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "sam",
        "speaker": "Sam",
        "sourceStart": 2985,
        "sourceEnd": 3094,
        "text": "Keep messages short and repeat them. That is my advice. Short messages are easier to understand and remember.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "1c119e6e8097b4191f4cc3c3f885b7e3a73e85cfaf21d6823829d2bece8a141e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3102,
        "sourceEnd": 3161,
        "text": "Thank you, panel. Next week, we will look at weather plans.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "5b3c4d04fbf9dbac94b3d68ae9fe37091c109f8873d6d9da398b70a01ab3f219",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
